BT 1 0 0 1 0 62 Tm -0.064567 Tw 12 TL /F1 10 Tf 0 0 0 rg (The ) Tj /F4 10 Tf (PickList) Tj /F1 10 Tf ( data type defines a property that can take one value from a predefined set of options. It is best suited) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.581794 Tw (for fields where only a single choice is valid at any given time. This ensures consistency and restricts inputs to) Tj T* 0 Tw .919653 Tw (known, valid values. This type is commonly used for categorical selections such as character class, item rarity, or) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.40894 Tw (region. By standardizing the input, PickList helps reduce errors and supports better validation and filtering within) Tj T* 0 Tw -0.010347 Tw (game systems. In user interfaces, a ) Tj /F4 10 Tf (PickList) Tj /F1 10 Tf ( is typically presented as a dropdown menu, allowing users to choose) Tj T* 0 Tw (only one option from the list.) Tj T* ET
