BT 1 0 0 1 0 518 Tm 12 TL /F5 10 Tf .501961 .501961 .501961 rg (# Eagerly resolves and validates all references in loaded documents.) Tj T* (# When enabled, this optimization ensures that all references in documents are resolved and validated) Tj T* (# during loading. This comes with a performance cost but guarantees the validity of references.) Tj T* /F4 10 Tf 0 0 0 rg (--optimizations) Tj .733333 .733333 .733333 rg ( ) Tj 0 0 0 rg (eagerReferenceResolution) Tj .733333 .733333 .733333 rg  T*  T* /F5 10 Tf .501961 .501961 .501961 rg (# Opts for raw references without generating helper methods for referenced documents.) Tj T* (# With this optimization, the generated code will not include helper methods for accessing) Tj T* (# referenced documents, keeping only accessors that work with raw references.) Tj T* /F4 10 Tf 0 0 0 rg (--optimizations) Tj .733333 .733333 .733333 rg ( ) Tj 0 0 0 rg (rawReferences) Tj .733333 .733333 .733333 rg  T*  T* /F5 10 Tf .501961 .501961 .501961 rg (# Avoids generating helper methods for localized strings, keeping only raw accessors.) Tj T* (# This optimization eliminates helper methods for accessing localized text, instead providing) Tj T* (# accessors that deal directly with lists of localized texts.) Tj T* /F4 10 Tf 0 0 0 rg (--optimizations) Tj .733333 .733333 .733333 rg ( ) Tj 0 0 0 rg (rawLocalizedTexts) Tj .733333 .733333 .733333 rg  T*  T* /F5 10 Tf .501961 .501961 .501961 rg (# Keeps text properties carrying a vector, rectangle or tags editor as plain strings.) Tj T* (# By default such a property is renamed to ') Tj (<) Tj (Name) Tj (>) Tj (Raw' and a parsed accessor taking its place) Tj T* (# is generated. This optimization skips the parsing helpers and leaves the property untouched.) Tj T* /F4 10 Tf 0 0 0 rg (--optimizations) Tj .733333 .733333 .733333 rg ( ) Tj 0 0 0 rg (rawCompositeTypes) Tj .733333 .733333 .733333 rg  T*  T* /F5 10 Tf .501961 .501961 .501961 rg (# Disables string pooling during game data loading.) Tj T* (# Turning off string pooling can yield a minor performance improvement at the cost of increased) Tj T* (# memory usage, as it avoids reusing short strings.) Tj T* /F4 10 Tf 0 0 0 rg (--optimizations) Tj .733333 .733333 .733333 rg ( ) Tj 0 0 0 rg (disableStringPooling) Tj .733333 .733333 .733333 rg  T*  T* /F5 10 Tf .501961 .501961 .501961 rg (# Disables generation of code for loading game data from JSON formatted files.) Tj T* (# This optimization omits code related to JSON serialization, useful when JSON formatted) Tj T* (# game data is not used.) Tj T* /F4 10 Tf 0 0 0 rg (--optimizations) Tj .733333 .733333 .733333 rg ( ) Tj 0 0 0 rg (disableJsonSerialization) Tj .733333 .733333 .733333 rg  T*  T* /F5 10 Tf .501961 .501961 .501961 rg (# Disables generation of code for loading game data from Message Pack formatted files.) Tj T* (# Similar to DisableJsonSerialization, this option removes code related to loading data) Tj T* (# from Message Pack formatted files.) Tj T* /F4 10 Tf 0 0 0 rg (--optimizations) Tj .733333 .733333 .733333 rg ( ) Tj 0 0 0 rg (disableMessagePackSerialization) Tj .733333 .733333 .733333 rg  T*  T* /F5 10 Tf .501961 .501961 .501961 rg (# Disables generation of code related to applying patches during game data loading.) Tj T* (# This removes a significant portion of code that is mainly used for modding support,) Tj T* (# where patches are applied to game data at runtime.) Tj T* /F4 10 Tf 0 0 0 rg (--optimizations) Tj .733333 .733333 .733333 rg ( ) Tj 0 0 0 rg (disablePatching) Tj .733333 .733333 .733333 rg  T*  T* /F5 10 Tf .501961 .501961 .501961 rg (# Disables generation of enums with known document IDs.) Tj T* (# This removes a significant portion of code that contains listings of IDs for) Tj T* (# documents known at the moment of code generation, which improves compilation time.) Tj T* /F4 10 Tf 0 0 0 rg (--optimizations) Tj .733333 .733333 .733333 rg ( ) Tj 0 0 0 rg (disableDocumentIdEnums) Tj .733333 .733333 .733333 rg  T* ET
